Text and identity: read in full in the registered American Presidency Project transcription (jobs/app-executive-orders/output/texts/executive-order-8897-exemption-miss-augusta-f-johnston-from-compulsory-retirement-for-age.txt; grade mirror_transcription, acceptable_as_original false; standing note: original not yet held; replace and re-check quotes when an official copy is retrieved). Page check per jobs/claim-kit/AGENT_PROTOCOL.md (working-text paragraph), done 2026-11-04: the APP mirror page record with the same sha256 in jobs/app-executive-orders/output/MIRROR_DOCUMENTS.jsonl (Common Crawl capture 2025-03-27T05:13:30Z) has the heading "Executive Order 8897—Exemption of Miss Augusta F. Johnston From Compulsory Retirement for Age", its date (1941-09-12) and subject agree with the held text, and its text_sha256 equals the held file's. Identity: the register lists this number with date 1941-09-12, signer Franklin D. Roosevelt and the title "Exemption of Augusta F. Johnston From Compulsory Retirement for Age"; the held text concerns Miss Augusta F. Johnston and ends with the signature "FRANKLIN D ROOSEVELT" and the date line "September 12, 1941.". Clauses are quoted from that registered file, not from the unregistered clause-drafts copy. The register title names "Augusta F. Johnston" while the APP heading and the held text name Miss Augusta F. Johnston; the number, date and one-person subject agree, so the identity holds.
Content: the order has one recital and one operative sentence. It exempts one named employee, Miss Augusta F. Johnston (administrative assistant, Public Roads Administration, Federal Works Agency), from compulsory retirement for age under section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), for a period of one year ending September 30, 1942. The recital says he "will reach the retirement age prescribed for automatic separation from the service" and asks that he "be exempted from compulsory retirement for age for a period of one year". The inventory is therefore one clause, the exemption. Extension reading: this order is the initial exemption; any later exemption of the same person would be a new exercise of the section 204 power with its own period and a later event, not an end of this order, and the packet's searches show none in the held texts.
Member checks: {"earlier_end_check":"No earlier end found. The only cessation source is the order's own period, \"one year ending September 30, 1942\". The packet's bounded number search of the held order texts (lookup scope: exactly held_texts(), clause-drafts excluded) found no other held text that cites Executive Order 8897. The Federal Register catalog disposition-note search (later-events:ofr_catalog, checked 2026-10-19) returned no hit for this order. The person-name search of the held order texts (namier:held_texts_person_name, checked 2026-10-28, whose leads list later or undated orders only) found no later order naming Miss Augusta F. Johnston. Statute check (the type rule research/readiness/type-rules/TR-RETIREMENT-EXEMPTION.json lists a change in the governing retirement statute as a possible earlier end): held APP exemption orders signed after this one still rest on the same section, for example EO 9271 of November 17, 1942 (\"section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby further exempt the said George T. Summerlin from compulsory retirement for age\") and EO 9530 of March 14, 1945 (\"section 204 of the act of June 30, 1932, 47 Stat. 382, 404 (U.S.C., title 5, sec. 715a), I hereby exempt the said Harry F. Hawley from compulsory retirement for age\"). Their wording shows that section 204 was still the authority for exemptions after this order's last day, so it had not been repealed. No held source shows that any amendment of section 204 extended or extinguished this order's dated exemption, and a later general rule is an end only with a reason it extinguished the command (owner ruling 2026-10-28). The employee's separation, retirement or death would end the practical use of the exemption but is not an instrument ending the command, and none is cited in the packet. Amendments are later events, not ends, and none is found.","independent_command_check":"None found. The order contains one command, the exemption of one named employee; it prescribes no report, procedure, delegation, appropriation or continuing duty. The compulsory-retirement rule it excepts comes from section 204 and the retirement statutes, which are independent of this order, so when the exemption's period ended no command of this order remained to continue.","savings_check":"The exemption is exhausted at 1942-09-30; its accrued effects (service, pay, retirement credit) are separate from the order and are stated as transferred_or_accrued. No later exemption order for the same person is found by the name search.","scope_check":"Scope: one named employee, Miss Augusta F. Johnston (administrative assistant, Public Roads Administration, Federal Works Agency). The dossier inventory has one whole-order clause (characters 0-692 of the registered file, the recital and the operative sentence); the signature and date line follow it in the full 732-character text. Nothing in the text is outside that clause, so no inventory correction is needed."}
